ically at $q_0$' (the documented 'canonical' <- 'numerical(ly)' substitution class); 'the formal derivation' -> the actual producer script name. A third likely instance in the same block: 'are real canonical constants unaffected by the algebraic action' -> 'are real numerical constants'. CONVENTION FLAG (separate, verified): the block defines $z = 1/(q^{1/2}+q^{-1/2})$, which equals sqrt(q)/(q+1) = 0.4993203342 at q_0 — this is the EXCISED convention C, not the canonical convention D z = q^3/(q^2+1) = 0.6126880371. It is written in the reciprocal-of-sum spelling that the detector-blindness taxonomy records as detector-invisible, and it survives inside content/ after the 2026-08-10 content-only drain. NOTATION FLAG: 'the average $\\Phi_1 := \\tfrac12(\\Phi_1(\\beta)+\\Phi_1(S(\\beta)))$' defines Phi_1 in terms of itself; it needs a distinct name (e.g. Phi_1^{even}).","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","notes":"MATH ERROR FOUND (sympy-verified, three independent ways). The block states 'The Frobenius antipode maps the primitive factor (c, d) to (c, d - c h_A)'. That map is NOT an involution and does NOT preserve det T, so it cannot be an antipode of an order-2 action and cannot support the block's own claim 'For each primitive the determinant is S-invariant': det T(c, d - c h_A) - det T(c,d) = -2 c d h_A, and applying it twice to (1,0) gives (1,-2h_A), not (1,0). It also contradicts Table 3, which lists S(1,-h_A) = (1,0) with det -1 — under the block's rule S(1,-h_A) = (1,-2h_A) with det 2h_A^2 - 1. The correct map, which is involutive, leaves det T identically invariant, and reproduces all three Table-3 rows exactly, is (c,d) -> (c, -c h_A - d). It agrees with the block's rule on (1,0) only, which is why the Phi_3 spot-check still came out right. Fix: replace 'to (c, d - c h_A)' with 'to (c, -c h_A - d)'. NOT applied inline: this is math, not prose.","history":3},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"folio-assistant-sci/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","notes":"block has no .lean sibling","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-branch-jargon","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"unknown","changed":["md: on disk, no hash recorded","ts: on disk, no hash recorded"],"at":"2026-08-08","reviewer":"agent","by":"local/one-voice-audit","notes":"[EXPIRED-NO-FIELD-HASH]